2026-09-24 M0 .claude/settings.json: Appendix C checked against current Claude Code docs — `:*` prefix rules and the hook schema are valid; `MultiEdit` no longer exists (harmless in the matcher, kept verbatim). Added deny rules for the GitHub MCP merge tools (mcp__github__merge_pull_request, mcp__github__enable_pr_auto_merge): cloud threads merge through MCP, not `gh`, so `Bash(gh pr merge:*)` alone didn't enforce "never merge". `Bash(git push --force:*)` is order-sensitive (misses `git push origin x --force`); the real force-push control is branch protection on main (docs/SPEC_ISSUES.md 7).
2026-09-24 M0 scripts/protected_check.py: `git diff --name-only --no-renames` — without it, renaming a protected file away listed only the new path and passed with no label (found in M0 testing; regression tests in tests/guard/test_protected.py).
2026-09-24 M0 scripts/guard_hook.py: guard runs via `uv run --frozen` — a plain `uv run` after an edit to pyproject.toml re-locked uv.lock and installed the new dependency before the guard could flag it (found in M0 testing; regression test in tests/guard/test_hook.py).
2026-09-24 Manzoor: L1-L6 all go into the Signal Lab (weights stay 0 until the Lab proves them, §4.10.5); capex US seed keeps all 61 tickers; REITs stay in the US universe; the Signal Lab (M8) runs right after M4, before the web app (M7).
2026-09-24 M0 universe snapshots: SEC answered 429 "Request Rate Threshold Exceeded" to the cloud session's shared egress IP for ~25 min, then 200; both snapshots were fetched from the session. Added .github/workflows/universe.yml (fetch on a runner, commit to the branch; needs the SEC_USER_AGENT secret) as the fallback and for rebuilds. fetch_fixtures.py gained `--source sec|nse`.
